    "fdaa252a061e27b93149c360661f95b27ce8c7fe": {
      "message": "fix(github): accept a pasted token and resolve the store per call\n\nThe setup card captured `ctx.credentials` while the plugin was applying: on a\nHost whose credential store mounted a moment later the capture was\n`undefined` for the life of the process, so `describe()` reported\n`importable: false` and the only button on the card was permanently disabled.\n\nThe bridge now reads the store on every call instead of once at mount, which\nis also what the token reader already did.\n\nThe same card showed `GITHUB_TOKEN=<令牌>` in a bordered `<code>` that read\nlike an input but could not be focused, and the only way in was the gh CLI.\nIt now holds a real password field: paste a classic or fine-grained token, the\nHost verifies it with `GET /user` before storing it (a rejected token never\noverwrites a working one), and the panel reports the login and its scopes.\n`POST /dsh-github/auth/token` carries the value, which never comes back to the\nbrowser.\n\nThe disabled state now says why it is disabled instead of going quiet.",
      "author": {
        "name": "litingyes",
        "email": "luz.liting@gmail.com"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "litingyes",
        "email": "luz.liting@gmail.com"
      },
      "committedAt": "2026-11-14T13:00:35+08:00",
