          "--- a/dsh-github/locale/en.json",
          "+++ b/dsh-github/locale/en.json",
          "@@ -3,3 +3,3 @@",
          "     \"title\": \"GitHub\",",
          "-    \"description\": \"GitHub inside DeepSeek Harness. The agent gets the official GitHub MCP server's full mcp__github__* tool set — repositories, issues, pull requests, reviews, checks, code search and notifications, readable and writable — and the right sidebar gains a GitHub tab that follows this Session's workspace repository and lists its issues, pull requests and notifications, with a detail view and a comment box. Write tools (create, update, merge, comment) ask for your approval before they run. The tab's import button copies the OAuth token the GitHub CLI already holds into the Harness credential store in one step; a GITHUB_TOKEN line in $DSH_HOME/.env works the same way. Requests carry your token straight to GitHub with no proxy in between. Only github.com is supported. Disabling the plugin removes the tools and the tab; the stored token stays where it is.\"",
          "+    \"description\": \"GitHub inside DeepSeek Harness. The agent gets the official GitHub MCP server's full mcp__github__* tool set — repositories, issues, pull requests, reviews, checks, code search and notifications, readable and writable — and the right sidebar gains a GitHub tab that follows this Session's workspace repository and lists its issues, pull requests and notifications, with a detail view and a comment box. Write tools (create, update, merge, comment) ask for your approval before they run. The tab accepts a pasted personal access token and can also copy the OAuth token the GitHub CLI already holds into the Harness credential store in one step; a GITHUB_TOKEN line in $DSH_HOME/.env works the same way. Requests carry your token straight to GitHub with no proxy in between. Only github.com is supported. Disabling the plugin removes the tools and the tab; the stored token stays where it is.\"",
          "   }"
