    "89b6b3f7dc8420abc0a85f8a6a05a6493b055cda": {
      "message": "fix(repo): let a never-released package through the tag gate\n\nA new plugin has no tag until its first release, so the gate painted the\nmerge commit red for a version that was not lost — it simply had not\nshipped yet. The rule now exempts exactly that case: a package with no\n`<dir>-v*` tag at all is reported as \"not published yet\" and passes.\n\nThe exemption ends at the first tag, which is the case the gate exists\nfor: once a package has one, every later version needs its own, or npm\nskips a number. Both halves are covered by tests.",
      "author": {
        "name": "litingyes",
        "email": "luz.liting@gmail.com"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "litingyes",
        "email": "luz.liting@gmail.com"
      },
